<article class="env-proposition" id="02L2">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02L2">Proposition <span data-tag="02L2">3.1.7.23</span>.</a> Let $f: X \rightarrow Y$ and $f': X' \rightarrow Y'$ be weak homotopy equivalences of simplicial sets. Then the induced map $(f \times f'): X \times X' \rightarrow Y \times Y'$ is also a weak homotopy equivalence. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      By virtue of Remark <a data-tag="00UD" href="/tag/00UD">3.1.7.16</a>, it will suffice to show that the morphisms $f \times \operatorname{id}_{X'}$ and $\operatorname{id}_{Y} \times f'$ are weak homotopy equivalences. We will give the proof for $f \times \operatorname{id}_{X'}$; the analogous statement for $\operatorname{id}_{Y} \times f'$ follows by a similar argument. Let $Z$ be a Kan complex; we wish to show that precomposition with $f$ induces a bijection 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \begin{eqnarray*}  \pi _0( \operatorname{Fun}(Y \times X', Z) ) &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \pi _0( \operatorname{Fun}(Y, \operatorname{Fun}(X',Z) ) ) \\ &amp;  \rightarrow &amp;  \pi _0( \operatorname{Fun}(X, \operatorname{Fun}(X',Z) ) ) \\ &amp;  \simeq &amp;  \pi _0( \operatorname{Fun}(X \times X', Z ) ). \end{eqnarray*}
</div>
<p>
       This follows from our assumption that $f$ is a weak homotopy equivalence, since the simplicial set $\operatorname{Fun}(X',Z)$ is a Kan complex (Corollary <a data-tag="00TN" href="/tag/00TN">3.1.3.4</a>). 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
</p></p></article>
